# bgp-mup-1 decoding test - MUP IPv4 NLRI via ze bgp decode
# Tests MUP ISD route type 1 with RD 0:65001:100, architecture type 1
#
# Wire bytes breakdown (draft-ietf-bess-mup-safi Section 3.1.1):
# 01 = architecture type 1 (3gpp-5g)
# 00 01 = route type 1 (Interwork Segment Discovery)
# 0c = length 12, the octets of the route type specific field
# 00 00 FD E9 00 00 00 64 = RD type 0: ASN=65001, value=100
# 18 = prefix length 24 bits
# 0a 00 00 = 10.0.0.0, the 3 significant octets of the prefix
stdin=payload:hex=0100010c0000fde900000064180a0000
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze bgp decode --json --nlri ipv4/mup -:stdin=payload
expect=json:json={ "arch": 1, "code": 1, "name": "InterworkSegmentDiscoveryRoute", "prefix_ip": "10.0.0.0", "prefix_ip_len": 24, "raw": "0100010C0000FDE900000064180A0000", "rd": "0:65001:100" }
